// WHY: locks FRAGO 002 cluster C1's SEVERITY case — no channel, no `background`, no
// `.copy()`, no `errors`. `rows` is an ordinary `array<int>` local declared before a
// `wait sleep(20)`, then passed as a plain argument to a function whose OWN body
// suspends (`wait sleep(1)`). Same producer as the channel-send probe in this
// cluster (`collect_crossings_in_stmts` skipping a suspending statement's own
// operands), reached through the plainest possible call form. This is ordinary
// code — the severity finding FRAGO 002 ranks ahead of the channel-transfer shape.
//
// Observed today (2026-09-06, default optimized mode, ynz-lang HEAD): silent wrong
// output, EXIT 0 — prints "6" where "3" is correct. Confirmed-live by dispatch
// hardening-p2b-20260905-a1 as probe D (target/p2b-probe/d_suspcall.ynz, gitignored).
// Closes M8 FR #11(a) via the same producer as the channel-send shape (also proves
// the defect is not "specific to the channel-transfer path" —
// `fuzz_grammar/mod.rs::take_or_make_array`'s doc comment claim is false).
//
// When C1's fix lands: exit 0, stdout exactly "3\nend\n".
function useRows(rows: array<int>) -> nothing {
  wait sleep(1)
  print(rows.count().toString())
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  let rows: array<int> = [10, 20, 30]
  wait sleep(20)
  useRows(rows)
  print(`end`)
}
